  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1031 AM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nAn incoming upper level trough will swing through the Central and\nNorthern Plains on Wednesday, and tries (but does not succeed) to\nbreak down the upper ridge over the southeast. At the same time, \nan upper level low becomes cut off and anchored over the Florida \npeninsula.\n\nThe cut-off low will keep our upper level winds mainly easterly \nthrough Thursday, reducing the true potential of how much we could\nwarm up. Friday, the southwesterly winds aloft ahead of the \ntrough to the north will give a slight push to temps though. \nRegardless, with the strength of the ridge, we will have slightly \nwarmer than normal temps, reaching the mid/upper 60s on Wednesday,\nwith a few of us reaching the lower 70s on Thursday and all of us\nin the 70s Friday and Saturday. Overnight lows will be above \nfreezing through the extended, upper 30s/lower 40s.",
